    "body": "## Accepted scope\n\nScoped status: claimed_solved, 4/5 author turns. The unchanged compact smooth genus-two-curve times elliptic-curve construction has h_J^- >= 3 and a nonintegrable almost-complex structure. Two full independent AI audits accept its exact proof. Generic vanishing remains the prior Tan-Wang-Zhang-Zhu theorem. No exact h_J^- value, fixed-symplectic-form compatibility, novelty or journal acceptance is claimed.\n\nAI-assisted and unrefereed. Independent AI review is not human peer review or formal proof certification. Includes authored mathematics, complete audits/acceptance, replay code and public verification metadata. No copied source documents, dataset contents or private coordination material are included. The existing QUEUE changes only this problem's Status, Turns and Findings cells; all other bytes are preserved.\n\n## External verification anchors\n\n- PUBLIC_MANIFEST.json SHA-256: `18b022a9f45f4b8194629cae8143f6be4884dbba51b7616cc64c1b7ab2cf7117`\n- verify_publication.py SHA-256: `994408c8bfb602939d03a8ed674f0aa06eed1e80477a473c17ddc8566e49aea5`\n\nAuthenticate these pins before executing downloaded code. Hash checks and finite controls do not independently prove the general mathematical claims. See attempts/30004549/README.md for the exact reproduction instructions and evidence boundaries.\n\nDraft only. Downloaded remote replay and exact-head hosted-check inspection are in progress; no hosted-CI pass is claimed.",
